R"VG(
# modern9.vg (H-04, the second pass): the scientific paper: the people's own world measured (its aquifers and moons, its ring, its comet
# and its lights, its dunes and ice, its herds' sicknesses and its birds' songs, its old pots and dyes), each sentence built from parts
# (what was done, where, with what; what came of it), each people's scholars with their own few habits of phrase (`people=K`).

genre.paper (words=21..72)
  {pp.title}\n{pp.abstract}\n{pp.result}\n{pp.end}
  {pp.title}\n{pp.abstract} {pp.method}\n{pp.result}\n{pp.end}
  {pp.title}\n{pp.abstract}\n{pp.result} {pp.result2}\n{pp.end}

pp.title (formula people=3)
  {pp.topic}: a study at {$home}.
  On {pp.topic}, with new measurements.
  {pp.topic}: {#n|year} of observations.
  Notes on {pp.topic}.
  A new account of {pp.topic}.
  {pp.topic}, reconsidered.
  Towards a theory of {pp.topic}.

pp.topic (share=0.6)
  the decline of the aquifer
  the motion of {moon.or}
  the yield of {crop} under changed conditions
  the spread of {pp.sick}
  the record of the weather over {n} decades
  the songs of the {bird}
  sickness in the {herd}
  the oldest houses of {$home}
  the glazes of the old {mod.pot}
  the dyes of the {craft} trade
  the age of {mountain}
  the {tree} of {land}
  the flight of the {bird}
  (comet=1) the orbit of the comet
  (aurora=1) the lights in the north
  (rings=1) the shadow of the ring
  (geysers=1) the hot springs of {mountain}
  (glacial=1) the retreat of the ice
  (erg=1) the march of the dunes
  (saltflats=1) the salt of the flats
  (companion=1) the second sun
  (coast=1) the {fish} of {sea}
  (coast=1 moons>0) the tides of {sea}
moon.or
  (moons>0) {moon}
  (moons=0) {star}
pp.sick
  (sick=1) the present sickness
  (sick=0) disease in the cities
  fever in the {herd}
mod.pot (people=2)
  pots
  jars
  bowls
  tiles
  cups
  plates

pp.abstract (share=0.8)
  We report {pp.what} over {#n|year} at {pp.where}{pp.rep2}.
  We report the results of a survey of {nbig} {pp.sites}.
  We revisit {pp.old} with {pp.new}.
  We compare the records of {$home} with those of {pp.other}, {pp.cmp2}.
  We describe a new method for {pp.measure}, and {pp.firstres}.
  We test an old saying of the {$home} markets: {proverb}.
pp.what (people=2)
  measurements made
  observations made
  counts made
  samples taken
  soundings taken
pp.where (people=3)
  {$home}
  the station at {$home}
  {holyplace}
  the {craft} works at {$home}
  the observatory at {$seat}
  (has:$home.landmark) {$home.landmark}
pp.rep2 (people=3)
  (2)
  , by hand
  , with the old instruments
  , in all weathers
  , with the help of students
pp.cmp2 (people=2)
  year by year
  season by season
  as far back as they go
  where they overlap
pp.sites (people=4)
  sites
  households
  fields
  springs
  schools
  herds of {herd}
  (coast=1) fishing boats
pp.old (people=2)
  the old observations
  the measurements of the founding years
  the records of {holyplace}
  the counts our grandparents made
pp.new (people=3)
  new instruments
  better maps
  a larger sample
  a new method
  the help of the {craft} guild
pp.other (people=2)
  {$seat}
  {city2}
  the coastal towns
  the hill country
pp.firstres (people=2)
  its first results
  what it found at once
  why it took so long
  what it cannot do
pp.measure (people=3)
  measuring the flow of {river}
  counting the {bird}
  dating old {material}
  weighing the {crop} harvest
  reading the old {mod.pot}

pp.method (share=0.8)
  Samples were taken at {n} sites along {river}{pp.meth2}.
  The instruments were built in the {craft} works at {$home}{pp.meth2}.
  (has:$home.landmark) Observations were made at night from {$home.landmark}{pp.meth2}.
  The measurements were made by schoolchildren and checked {pp.checked}.
  The counts were made {time.of}, every day for a year.
pp.meth2 (people=2)
  (2)
  , in all weathers
  , over {#n|season}
  , by hand
pp.checked (people=2)
  twice
  by the station staff
  against the old tables

pp.result (share=0.8)
  The trend is clear and {pp.trendx}{pp.restail}.
  The results agree with {pp.pred} to within {pp.within}.
  The results do not agree with any {pp.model} we have {pp.tried}.
  The effect is small but {pp.small}{pp.restail}.
  We find a cycle of about {#n|year}, {pp.cyc}.
  The old account is wrong in {pp.wrong}{pp.restail}.
  The data support the older view, {pp.surp}.
  The {bird} {pp.birdv} {#n|day} earlier than {pp.ago}.
  The yield of {crop} fell by a {nth} where {pp.cause2}.
  (stage>=0) The trend, if it continues, will be serious within {pp.gen}.
  (stage>=1) The trend has continued. We have stopped calling it a trend.
pp.restail (people=3)
  (2)
  , as feared
  , and nobody is surprised
  , in every district
  , and older than we thought
  , and the farmers saw it first
pp.within (people=2)
  the error
  a hair
  a day
  a hand's width
pp.tried (people=2)
  tried
  heard of
  dared to publish
pp.ago (people=2)
  a century ago
  in the founding years
  our grandparents said
  the old almanacs say
pp.trendx (people=2)
  accelerating
  steady
  slowing
  seasonal
pp.pred (people=2)
  the predictions
  the old tables
  the farmers' calendar
  the observatory's figures
pp.model (people=2)
  model
  table
  theory
  explanation
pp.small
  real
  growing
  clear
  worrying
  stubborn
  everywhere
  older than the town
pp.cyc (people=4)
  as the old almanacs said
  which nobody had noticed
  tied to {moon.or}
  tied to the {crop} harvest
  close to a lifetime
  longer than the records
  that the {herd} keepers swear by
pp.wrong (people=2)
  almost every particular
  its dates
  its causes
  everything but its conclusion
pp.surp (people=2)
  to our surprise
  against our expectation
  which will please the {craft} guild
  which will please nobody
pp.birdv (people=2)
  return
  nest
  leave
pp.cause2 (people=2)
  the water table dropped
  the {herd} grazed
  the winters were warm
  the old channels silted up
pp.gen (people=2)
  a generation
  our lifetimes
  {#n|decade}

pp.result2 (share=0.8)
  We cannot yet say why.
  A larger study {pp.larger}.
  The belief, as it turns out, is {pp.half} right.
  The {bird} noticed it before we did.
  The {pp.who2} of {$home} knew it {pp.already}.
pp.larger (people=3)
  is under way at {$seat}
  has been promised by {ruler.the}
  needs money nobody has offered
  will begin in {season.next}
  is planned with the {craft} guild
pp.who2 (people=3)
  farmers
  herders
  old women
  {craft} workers
  children
  (coast=1) fishermen
pp.already
  already
  all along
  for generations
pp.half (people=2)
  half
  mostly
  partly
  entirely

pp.end (formula people=3)
  Further work is needed.
  We thank the station staff, who worked through {season.now}.
  The data are kept at {$home}.
  We thank the keepers of {holyplace} for the old records.
  We thank the people of {$home}, who put up with us.
  (stage>=1) Funding for this work has been withdrawn.
)VG"
